  "sections": {
    "1": {
      "purpose": "Purpose: This Interface Requirements Specification (IRS) defines the interface requirements for the ground segment and sensor interfaces of the Defence R&D software project.  The IRS outlines the functional and performance specifications for each interface, ensuring interoperability between ground segment components and sensor data acquisition systems.\n\nNote: The IRS is based on the following source documents:\n\nIRS_v2.0.docx: Interface Requirements Specification (IRS) Revision 2.0\nMoM_DesignReview04.docx: Minutes of Meeting \u2014 Design Review 04",
      "scope": "Scope: This Interface Requirements Specification (IRS) defines the interface requirements for the ground segment and sensor interfaces of the Defence R&D software project. The IRS outlines the functionality, data format, and communication protocols required for seamless interaction between the ground segment and the sensor interfaces. It also details specific requirements related to telemetry acquisition, health reporting, and sensor data transmission.\n\nSource: REQ-0001 (for MTBF estimate)\nREQ-0002 (for MTBF estimate)\nREQ-0005 (for REST interface versioning)\nREQ-0006 (for structured JSON logging output)\nREQ-0008 (for authentication mechanism confirmation)\n\nNote: This IRS is based on the design review minutes from Design Review 04, which can be accessed in MoM_DesignReview04.docx.  It also references specific requirements outlined in the project's initial documentation and related documents like api.proto for data format definitions.",
