      "encoding": "ICD Section 3. Message Formats and Data Structures - Encoding Rules\n\n3.1 Encoding Rules\n\nThis section outlines the encoding rules for data transmitted between system components, adhering to the specified message formats defined in the API protocol (api.proto).  The following encoding rules apply:\n\nTelemetry Sample Envelopes: The ground segment interface transmits telemetry sample envelopes using the TelemetrySample message defined in the api.proto file.\n    * This message format is consistent with Interface Requirement IR-0101.\nAcquisition Command Interface:  The acquisition command interface accepts commands to start acquisition, utilizing the StartCommand message defined in the api.proto file.\n    * This message format is consistent with Interface Requirement IR-0102.\nHealth Reporting Interface: The health reporting interface exposes MTBF estimates using the HealthReport message defined in the api.proto file.\n    * This message format is consistent with Interface Requirement IR-0103.\n\n3.2 Data Structure Encoding\n\nThe data structure encoding rules are based on the following:\n\nProto3 Protocol: The messages are encoded using the proto3 protocol defined in the api.proto file.\nMessage Format Consistency: All message formats adhere to the specified message definitions and data structures as outlined in the API protocol (api.proto).\n\nNote: This section provides a high-level overview of the encoding rules for this project. Further details on specific encoding techniques, error handling, and communication protocols will be provided in subsequent sections."
    },
